[{"id":"VRCE-5-52-1","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":1,"english":"Casting his eyes on Lankā, the monkey, his wish attained, increasing his person and bursting with spirits, considered as to how to give the coup de grace to his exertions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052001","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2daa144620249dbb6bb54173ac63821bc55e85c5220c24f5f6b08fb8ff5b7336","compact":"3632cd7747548f250d82754298f83c6d4731d19267bf2b09af7e433b8e1f4129","nasal":"18646197c6a33b18dfe0e230bcfe28fc02c633eb0dc70b7ad84186d2eddb41bd"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-52-2","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":2,"english":"What recently is to done by me here to finish this business, that may afflict them the more?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052002","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9c214185b68a9379cb270d53e59cc6c0c873731334a1b0e2ceadc6253edb1891","compact":"b8f8f9cbe509c0fba17a0a231a663481aa471591e2a964444204ddaad877c5e3","nasal":"e7e71b61ee94494067eb4d08d72d16613443e563bff7960ae59fdb259e7df0ee"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-52-3","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":3,"english":"I have ravaged the wood, and slain the choice Rākşasas, and destroyed by main force a portion of the army. Now it remains to demolish the fortifications.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052003","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"66136ba49b9c6f3fbe70d6b5d55a6d2d78bf92999367a4d34c412cee09f8c945","compact":"8915987df216c7fe62b47cf4741c1a8252cc88ba264d18754a6aa3a2abb30dfe","nasal":"8915987df216c7fe62b47cf4741c1a8252cc88ba264d18754a6aa3a2abb30dfe"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-52-4","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":4,"english":"On the fortifications being destroyed, my work shall nave its toils crowned with joy. By undergoing slight labour in this business, I shall have my pains furnished with fruit.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052004","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bab8945498191a140aae9c35dfc963b0e9ec825fd4d31c84a2c4cc29c2f825d1","compact":"308db8363167e700a81fabf69de762c9652b1876c756c082699f035aabc32fcc","nasal":"308db8363167e700a81fabf69de762c9652b1876c756c082699f035aabc32fcc"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-52-5","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":5,"english":"That bearer of sacrificial offerings (Vide ante) who flame on my tail, it is my duty to propitiate him with these excellent edifices.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052005","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d861d0789a8546eff0b0b17fc24bf8ce9825453bf895cd2075d19418fce5b3bf","compact":"12f84a573474cd336197ac5d57142e44a3540215ede6c5ca3ec6af68e929a9e4","nasal":"2712f05b2fe0586183fdf126f29eea5519592d7aefdcf61fbdead049dca59969"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-52-6","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":6,"english":"Thereat that mighty monkey, with his tail aglow, and resembling a cloud (luminous) with lightning, began to range before the dwellings in Lankā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.86,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052006","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"368515d7f03c5f2ff9b33983bb965c1725e5ecd0417315557b5a39656a3ed356","compact":"912c81cd4688350ffa669d0a31fef49639727c77cf923034448ed0d54b25f949","nasal":"833a366d319d0c83b192f17a7ed2ef8aa683ae7dc49041f6768dce616e55d766"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-52-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":7,"english":"And that one gifted with exceeding vehemence, and in strength resembling the Wind, bounding up set fire to the dwelling of Prahasta. Then Hanuman endowed with prowess, leaping up, set to Mahaparsva's mansion fire resembling that at the universal dissolution.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.652,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2977ea9856e6906400557dc71987d886e5751a248084c0897a0410f927129d51","compact":"f8376e65ee7a7721fe20c9e73956de9026bc26eb8372e0d90e4d0a471802d0fd","nasal":"f8376e65ee7a7721fe20c9e73956de9026bc26eb8372e0d90e4d0a471802d0fd"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-52-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":8,"english":"And assisted by the wind, that highly powerful and vehement one (Fire) flaimed up, like fire at the wreck of all, and the fire attained energy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.868,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"db617b10f5ad696287f45551b7bf149de53e3c991e832e320b470cba7537f3a2","compact":"fc139476b706de2b04f4067f1aec82880f04738d2ebc9e549a9d3a55fec6d026","nasal":"fc139476b706de2b04f4067f1aec82880f04738d2ebc9e549a9d3a55fec6d026"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-52-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":9,"english":"The wind spreading the flaming fire all round those dwellings, those mansions furnished with golden networks; and containing pearls and gems; enjewelled and magnificent, were shorn of their splendour.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.931,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052009","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a54add48d70c63f2d8feb3dbee585c2c06507af7a390428058289981b46a8468","compact":"7abdd218cbc5ab80ba8779f0a605f417ab4a044b91b6773f0968fceec7e273d3","nasal":"7abdd218cbc5ab80ba8779f0a605f417ab4a044b91b6773f0968fceec7e273d3"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-52-10","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":10,"english":"The wind spreading the flaming fire all round those dwellings, those mansions furnished with golden networks; and containing pearls and gems; enjewelled and magnificent, were shorn of their splendour.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.825,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052010","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f378ebf0e271c15f036c75c80be1e493579ff861ce6c9a8a0a54349cbe55c124","compact":"4e49d60587c447a3c3e5a5cdf77bd19421843e8a99a446aa82e7d423b2029155","nasal":"54f808a9b6f7c37e6f37a599bc5b848082fb290eaa3ece9b5fe04b14ae100fb4"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-52-11","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":11,"english":"The wind spreading the flaming fire all round those dwellings, those mansions furnished with golden networks; and containing pearls and gems; enjewelled and magnificent, were shorn of their splendour. And cracked edifices began to topple down to the ground, like the mansions of Siddhās falling from the firmament of the exhaustion of their righteousness. And there arose a mighty uproar of those Rākşasas, as, bereft of their good fortune, despairing of preserving their abodes, they rushed in all directions, \"Forsooth it is Fire himself that has come hither in the form of a monkey.” And females crying with babes on their breasts, suddenly plunged (into the fire).","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.467,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-16","DUTT-5-54-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052011","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1cf31b5effe1597fd1eaf950faa05d2dee4f23ccf8e8f4f8205486e9fd160bcb","compact":"67bfafdf06b93e69f407794df5963dc4f98c3c3055ea1aabed4e2abd1f244d34","nasal":"fef124621faebad82a8b4b5a7aad349778a90346b5ce9698c35b36f8eaa409f9"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-52-12","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":12,"english":"And he (Hanuman) saw various kinds of metals, mixed with diamonds, and coral, and lapises and pearls and silver, running down in streams from the mansions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.884,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052012","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ade7e37eeec56f216ba02d957b928c62b5270ef04cad70901de42e28f8daedb6","compact":"0de88158af89b86210ebf81b247853ed91eb83aa9034585067c226e94130ec23","nasal":"bbaa294f2543cf716d135a87e5d75dfac9f6407fdd25c4ffdf91c133e93a7acc"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-52-13","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":13,"english":"And as Fire is not cloyed with wood and straw, Hanumān never at all felt satiety on slaying those foremost of Räkşasas. And the Earth could not contain the Rākşasas slain by Hanumăn.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052013","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a0acb71a970b0bead82d60c50d89f9a37394a968755391af70db5209dc66e4f4","compact":"b8f9b6e44e9d99143ab8a14410be44f7840e71c691d892607edc40ec5984b14e","nasal":"49e868dc4b3a9528060d76e88a99fd2cffafe1c65f301b69483c7a2c9f995f19"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-52-14","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":14,"english":"And with the flames encircling her, and her foremost heroes fallen, and her warriors destroyed, Lankā, overcome by the might of Hanumān's wrath, became as if she had been blighted by an imprecation.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.89,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052014","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"469eb7684b1964e5ae36ce3637cda97aa5daf2e3f8773118398fd5294d15b75e","compact":"e670b5591b5346721619c405c106bfc9638210676f322797b6b4abc88c8e5306","nasal":"d25f1be473b4c488220c973be729d7a5fec0c0b84afd6e2951339f707e0faf53"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-52-15","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":15,"english":"Then the mighty-minded Hanumān beheld the Rākşasas in terror and trepidation and cast down, and Lankā marked by fire and bright flames, even as the Self-sprung eye the world destroyed by his rage.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.824,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052015","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ce679651c0e01d1b4f3e2304de2cd1128f7f0d71ba697d3ebbf3248065746989","compact":"587534dfb594dc41b575fd4cac84f011632d411b51bb5418a429254f50c5fc66","nasal":"a8e341063bef97dfe4bcd60ac29ca3e448d5bade2927906c5e47151fd039e7f0"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-52-16","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":16,"english":"And destroying many a Rākṣasa, felling many trees in the forest and setting fire to the houses of the Raksasas, the high-souled (monkey) became engaged in thoughts touching Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.911,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052016","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6ebeda22eb5a65b19d80626608145f35b2cbef710fa58a56c9c884f92d5da199","compact":"184e48cb06d97d53376d49e9a1e9f322bd9ae1b85735d667f6868ebda30ae086","nasal":"bb106e27dc4617f7c2f126d25643d58fd1dfcf6531111c14c12f77c457ee24ae"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-52-17","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":52,"verse":17,"english":"And having consumed ihe city of Lankä, the great monkey quenched the fire of his tail in the Ocean.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.609,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-54-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5052017","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3d2824f96206087537b065aefadf7f74316ac932d89b183a7c1f256999fb8a71","compact":"c3769294e645a7df4a3952b3200303ba6f5b005b86237fb82dd191fef466deac","nasal":"ebafa3de924c9ba6220c7fd1db02b030c87d3d78c00bed624b24ad0053e502ca"}}]
